  "id": "6d4db790-e339-465e-a6d0-7e4038a7606d",
  "title": "Cross-Model Attribute Selection for Vision-Language Models",
  "summary": "Both reports highlight the importance of attribute selection in vision-language models (VLMs) by emphasizing the need to avoid class names and use image-based attributes to improve interpretable zero-shot classification. They both focus on distribution shift and demonstrate how attribute prompts can be effectively selected by leveraging image data.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "arXiv AI reports on attributes should come from images, not class names, leading to improved interpretability in zero-shot classification.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Class-name-free attribute prompts achieve 23.8% accuracy on ImageNet, outperforming LLM-based descriptors by 3 points.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both studies demonstrate that attribute selection is a key factor in achieving efficient and interpretable model performance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
